{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":7815,"duration_api_ms":7802,"num_turns":1,"result":"\n\n# Feature: Prime Checker Script\n\n## Description\nCreate a standalone Python script `is_prime.py` at the project root that implements a primality-checking function using trial division and prints results for integers 1 through 20 when executed directly. This is the sole deliverable for the project.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] File `is_prime.py` exists at the project root\n- [ ] Defines `is_prime(n: int) -> bool` that returns `True` for prime `n`, `False` otherwise\n- [ ] Edge cases: `n <= 1` returns `False`; `n == 2` returns `True`; even `n > 2` returns `False`\n- [ ] Uses trial division with only odd divisors from 3 to `math.isqrt(n)` (step 2)\n- [ ] `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` block prints `is_prime(n)` for each `n` in 1–20, formatted as `{n}: {result}` (e.g., `1: False`, `2: True`)\n- [ ] Runs without errors on Python 3.8+ with no external dependencies\n- [ ] Output matches known primes in 1–20: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `is_prime.py` — Create new file containing the `is_prime()` function and `__main__` block\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: none\n- Blocks: none (this is the only feature in scope)\n\n---","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7c0894b0-4324-4dc4-aeca-8b9b064e8e9a","total_cost_usd":0.07793775,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10449,"cache_read_input_tokens":6433,"output_tokens":376,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10449,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":376,"cacheReadInputTokens":6433,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10449,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.07793775,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state